@page "/faq"

<PageTitle>Questions and answers - GigHaus</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Answers about hosting a house concert with GigHaus: what it costs, how privacy works, how many guests you need and how contributions work." />
</HeadContent>

<section class="mk-page-head">
    <div class="mk-wrap mk-narrow">
        <p class="mk-kicker">FAQ</p>
        <h1>Good questions.</h1>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mk-section">
    <div class="mk-wrap mk-narrow mk-faq">
        <details open>
            <summary>Is GigHaus really free?</summary>
            <p>Yes. There's no charge to use GigHaus, and it takes no cut of what guests contribute.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>What counts as a venue?</summary>
            <p>Any private space where people can sit and listen: a living room, a barn, a backyard, a basement. There's no minimum size.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Who can see my address?</summary>
            <p>The public show page only shows your city and state. GigHaus emails your street address to a guest after you confirm them. GigHaus can also see it so we can review your venue.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Why does my venue need approval?</summary>
            <p>We review each new venue so guests can trust what they find here. You can set up your venue and draft shows right away, then publish once you're approved.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Do I have to find the artist myself?</summary>
            <p>Yes. GigHaus doesn't find or book artists. You arrange the artist yourself and add them to your show.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Do artists and guests need accounts?</summary>
            <p>No. Only hosts sign in. You add the artist to your show, and guests reserve with just a name and email address.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>How do guests pay?</summary>
            <p>Guests contribute at the door. You set a suggested donation, or a minimum if one is required to attend, and the show page says clearly which it is. GigHaus doesn't take online payments yet.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Are contributions tax-deductible?</summary>
            <p>No. Contributions support the artist and the event. They aren't charitable donations and aren't tax-deductible.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
            <summary>Is there anything I should check before hosting?</summary>
            <p>It's worth checking your lease, homeowners' association rules, insurance and local noise rules, and letting your neighbors know. GigHaus can't give legal advice, so ask a professional if you're unsure.</p>
        </details>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="mk-section mk-section--gold">
    <div class="mk-wrap mk-closer">
        <Mascot Size="192" />
        <div>
            <h2>Still wondering about something?</h2>
            <a class="mk-btn mk-btn--navy" href="contact">Ask us</a>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
